ts³11100585947³1version³13³1cache_oldmajor³118³1cache_oldauthor³118³1cache_diff_default_author³11³1revision³119³1text_default³1ip³2217.247.139.242³2ts³21100585947³2version³21³2name³2text_default³2data³2summary³3*³3text³3= <nowiki>AnCap</nowiki> Wiki Icon Project =

Create an icon for the upper-right-hand corner of each page. To vote for one, bump its vote count. Use the "Upload" link at the top or bottom of the page if you don't have another place on the web to put your image file. The upload directory is http://billstclair.com/uploads/ . If that doesn't work (some browsers don't support uploading files), email your image to BillStClair, and he'll add it to this page.

http://billstclair.com/usemod.gif Votes: 0

The [[Ama-gi]] is an ancient Sumerian cuneiform word meaning "freedom". It is believed to be the first instance of humans writing that concept down. (Matt Apple has made a black and gold version of this, but hasn't managed to get it to BillStClair yet for posting). BillStClair installed this temporarily, because he likes it better than the "Use Mod" icon.

http://billstclair.com/Amagi.png Votes: 0

[[Matt Apple]]: What about something like this(minus the blue border of course):

upload:ama-gi-icon.jpg Votes: 0


BillStClair: I cropped Matt's icon, and installed the cropped version at the top of the page. What do people think?

http://billstclair.com/ama-gi-icon-cropped.png Votes: 0
